# Day 3: Long-ass car ride to Daocheng

Today was just a long-ass car ride from Shangri-la to Daocheng. The roads were
pretty bumpy and the driver was definitely speeding. There is actually a good
reason for the speeding, though. We had to go through this one road two-way road
that was turned into a one-way road due to construction. However, since people
still need to drive in both directions, a timed closure was implmeented. This
means that the road would go one way for a set period of time, then the
direction would reverse for another set period of time. We were originally told
that we had to use the road between 12PM to 2PM, but it turned out that we were
supposed to go *before* 12PM instead––hence the speeding. We aimed to arrive
after 12PM but now needed to reach before 12PM, or we would have to wait until
after 6PM to be able to use that stretch of the road again. In the end, we
arrived just in time to use the road and didn't have to find something to do to
kill time until 6PM.

